    "id": "train-287",
    "question": "Bran's tuition fee is $90. He does a part-time job that pays him $15 per month and he has a scholarship that takes care of 30% of his tuition fee. If he needs to pay his tuition fee within 3 months, how much does Bran still need to pay?",
    "gold": "18",
    "answer": "Bran's scholarship pays $90 x 0.30 = $<<90*0.30=27>>27 to his tuition fee.\nSo, the total amount he still needs to pay is $90 - $27 = $<<90-27=63>>63.\nAnd Bran will be able to earn $15 x 3 = $<<15*3=45>>45 after working for 3 months.\nTherefore, the total amount he still needs to pay is $63 - $45 = $<<63-45=18>>18.\n#### 18"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much Bran still needs to pay for his tuition fee, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the amount of the scholarship.\n2. Determine the total amount Bran earns from his part-time job over 3 months.\n3. Calculate the total amount Bran has after receiving the scholarship and his earnings.\n4. Subtract the total amount Bran has from his tuition fee to find out how much he still needs to pay.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail:\n\n1. Calculate the amount of the scholarship:\n   The scholarship covers 30% of the tuition fee.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Scholarship} = 0.30 \\times 90 = 27\n   \\]\n\n2. Determine the total amount Bran earns from his part-time job over 3 months:\n   Bran earns $15 per month from his part-time job.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Earnings from part-time job} = 15 \\times 3 = 45\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the total amount Bran has after receiving the scholarship and his earnings:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total amount} = 90 + 27 + 45 = 162\n   \\]\n\n4. Subtract the total amount Bran has from his tuition fee to find out how much he still needs to pay:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Amount still needed} = 90 - 162 = -72\n   \\]\n   Since the result is negative, it means Bran has more money than he needs to pay the tuition fee. The amount he still needs to pay is $0.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}\n\\]",
